A||||9||Songman||For Sale - 87 Monte Carlo SS Aerocoupe||||1||
Z||000000||Songman||08-26-2001||06:56 PM||||I hate to do it but my girlfriend wants a new Jeep Cherokee...Gonna sell my Aerocoupe to get her one...<P>If anyone is interested, e-mail me.<P>The car is white with tan interior and gold stripes. T-tops. 305HO with 200R4 tranny. All original except for wheels. Has a crappy set of Cragar SSTs on it. This car is very clean under the hood, and fairly clean on the inside. The carpet is badly stained from the previous owner. I am the second owner of this car.<P>The car has been sitting for about 6 months. Has some exhaust leaks due to broken exhaust manifold studs. I start it once a week to let it keep the battery up and the oil circulated. I parked it because it has a problem that happens sometimes but not all the time... sometimes under load it will just start sputtering and backfiring. I attribute this to the electronic distributor but I just have never replaced it. Gas prices went up and I started driving my Fieros.<P>If you aren't familiar with an Aerocoupe, it was a special edition Monte Carlo SS built only for two years in low numbers. It was built so Chevy could run the car on the NASCAR track. In these years the new Thunderbirds with the aerodynamic back were killing everything else. By 88 the Luminas were introduced and the Monte Carlos were no more, until later anyway...<P>In 87, there were 6052 Monte Carlo SS Aerocoupes built. These were built by C&C that some of us know because of our T-Top Fieros. <P>I was going to modify this car and even went so far as to buy a 454 GM crate motor for it, but my friends convinced me that it should be left original because of the rarity of it. There is one more rarity that I have no been able to disprove yet. Every white Aerocoupe I have seen so far has had red stripes and red interior in it. The tan interior and gold stripes was intended for black cars. This car was done like this from the factory. Don't know if it was a fluke or special order.<P>I am asking $4000 for the car. The price is firm. I will answer any questions by e-mail but I would want any prospective buyer to come check the car out before a deal is made...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||08-26-2001||08:12 PM||||If I was sunk in this Fiero, I'd love to have it! The aero coupe is one of my all time favorite cars. I have a friend that wants one, I will let him know. I hope it goes to a good home. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||08-26-2001||08:36 PM||||Thanks Cooter.. Yeah, I want someone to get it that will appreciate what it is too... If no one picks it up I'll just figure out another way to get her the Cherokee and keep it. It is one of my all-time favorite cars... You surely don't see anyone else driving a car like yours when you are in an Aerocoupe!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||7
